WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.002
RAGGlass · See inside your RAG.
A practical tour: upload → ask → check the PDF source.
Real local inference · PDF + retrieved evidence + answer.

00:00:04.002 --> 00:00:09.071
Step 1 / Upload a PDF
Click Upload PDF, choose the sample, and wait for Indexed.
This recording reuses the sample's existing index.

00:00:09.071 --> 00:00:18.344
Step 2 / Ask a document question
Type your question, then click Retrieve & answer.
Inspect the retrieved passages beside the live model's answer.

00:00:18.344 --> 00:00:25.576
Step 3 / Follow the citation
Click the source link → page 2. Verify 30 MB in the table.
The backend maps the retrieved chunk ID to the original PDF page.

00:00:25.576 --> 00:00:30.689
Step 4 / Inspect parsed evidence
Open Parsed content; compare the table, chunk ID, and page.
Source boxes are item bounds, not exact text spans.

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:35.768
Step 5 / Review the run settings
Expand Run settings & prompt to inspect the saved configuration.
Check the prompt, model, retrieval settings, and stage timings.

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:41.756
Step 6 / Test an unsupported question
Ask about annual electricity cost; check the refusal.
The document cannot confirm it; this run has no citations.

00:00:41.756 --> 00:00:46.982
Step 7 / Reopen a saved run
Open Run history, select a past query, and revisit its evidence.
The question, answer, evidence, and settings remain saved locally.

00:00:46.982 --> 00:00:54.732
Your turn / Reproduce the workflow
Try the CC0 PDF and six questions with your own model service.
Share a reproducible issue; star RAGGlass if it helps your work.
